    "body": "The medium puzzle today felt like a step up, but it was so much fun to untangle. I started by looking for the most restrictive rules. There was a greater than 5 constraint at 1,0, which meant that cell had to be a 6. Looking at my dominoes, I saw the 1,6 and 6,6. I paired the 1,6 domino at 2,0 and 1,0 because that 1 at 2,0 helped me satisfy the sum of 5 at the bottom left when combined with a 4 at 3,0.\n\nThe trickiest part was the equals region involving 1,2, 1,3, and 2,3. All three had to have the same number. By looking at what was left in my pile, I realized they all needed to be 5s. This allowed me to place the 5,5 domino at 1,2 and 1,3. From there, I focused on the sum of 12 in the bottom right. Using the 6,6 domino for 3,2 and 3,3 meant those two 6s plus a 0 at 2,2 perfectly hit that target. It is all about finding those anchor points and working outward!",
