    "body": "Wow, the hard puzzle today was a real brain teaser! Rodolfo Kurchan really outdid himself with this layout. I spent a good few minutes just staring at the board before I found my way in. The breakthrough for me was the bottom row. I saw the sum of 12 at 5,3 and 5,4 which immediately told me those had to be 6s. At the same time, the sum of 0 at 4,5 and 5,5 meant both of those had to be 0s. Having those 6s and 0s locked down gave me the courage to tackle the rest.\n\nThe most interesting part was the huge unequal region in the middle. It covers seven cells, and since we only use numbers 0 through 6, it means every single number must appear exactly once in that zone! That was the key to placing the middle dominoes. I had to be really careful with the equals constraint at 1,0, 2,0, and 3,0, making sure they matched up while not breaking the sums around them. I actually went down a wrong path once and had to back up, but seeing the 4,4 and 5,5 dominoes finally fit into their spots was such a great feeling. If you are stuck, look at the greater than constraints at the bottom left; they really help narrow down which high-value dominoes go where.",
